# prebuilds/linux-x64

Node tag: `linux` + `x64` (Linux x86_64).
Typical EPICS copy source: `linux-x86_64`.

## Build environment (fill in when packaging)

- OS:
- gcc/g++ / Node:
- EPICS base: 7.0.10
- pvxs: 1.5.2
- libevent: 2.1

Runtime loads `pvxs.node` **only** from this directory (not `build/Release`).
After copy, run `normalize-linux-libs.sh` to shorten sonames, rewrite NEEDED/SONAME, and set `$ORIGIN`.

## Files to copy here

From `npm run build`:

- `./build/Release/pvxs.node`

From EPICS / pvxs / libevent (versioned names are OK; the script renames them):

- `libpvxs.so.1.5` (or `libpvxs.so`)
- `libCom.so.3.25.0` (or `libCom.so`)
- `libevent_core-2.1.so.7.0.1` (or `libevent_core-2.1.so.7`)
- `libevent_pthreads-2.1.so.7.0.1` (or `libevent_pthreads-2.1.so.7`)

Search hints: `pvxs/lib/<arch>`, `base/lib/<arch>`, `pvxs/bundle/usr/<arch>/lib`.

After the script, the directory should contain short names only:

- `pvxs.node`
- `libpvxs.so`
- `libCom.so`
- `libevent_core.so`
- `libevent_pthreads.so`

## Fix library paths

Requires `patchelf`. From this directory:

```bash
cd prebuilds/linux-x64
bash ../../scripts/normalize-linux-libs.sh
```

The script will:

1. Rename versioned `.so` files to short names
2. `patchelf --replace-needed` (match your `readelf -d` NEEDED entries)
3. `patchelf --set-soname` on each bundled library
4. `patchelf --set-rpath '$ORIGIN'` on `pvxs.node` and each `.so`

If your EPICS build uses different version suffixes, edit the rename/`replace-needed` lists in the script.

## Self-test

From the package root (after `normalize-linux-libs.sh`; no `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`):

```bash
node -e "console.log(require('.').version())"
```
